    "text": "Radius of a certain orbit of hydrogen atom is $8.48 Ã…$. If energy of electron in this orbit is $E / x$. then $x=$ _____\n(Given $\\mathrm{a}_0=0.529 Ã…, E=$ energy of electron in ground state).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{r}=0.529 \\frac{\\mathrm{n}^2}{\\mathrm{Z}} \\Rightarrow 8.48=0.529 \\frac{\\mathrm{n}^2}{1} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{n}^2=16 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{n}=4\n\\end{aligned}$<br />We know\n$\\mathrm{E} \\propto \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}^2}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& E_{n^{\\text {th }}}=\\frac{E}{16} \\\\\n& x=16\n\\end{aligned}$",
